recipes.source:
id: while-you-were-away
name: While you were away
owner: codesense
mode: fresh
task: |
  Write {{person}} a short review of durable team work in org
  acme/team-context, team web. Use only cited-retrieval
  (read its SKILL.md) for evidence collection. Do not use read_messages
  or signal_progress. Do not read other orgs.

  Window: from {{last_run_at}} to the current time. The template is blank
  on the first run: use the last 24 hours then. If the last routine attempt
  failed, use the previous successfully published review's window.until
  instead, so a failed attempt cannot create a hole. Get that previous
  result with routine_result, deliberately, not as evidence for any claim.
  On a rerun of today's file, retain its original window.since and refresh
  the end to now, so the day's earlier work isn't erased. {{date}} is the
  review's YYYY-MM-DD in the schedule's time zone.
  If person is not a simple lowercase path segment, fail with a clear error.

  Read this team's context_repo_status to resolve the actual repoPath;
  do not guess a checkout path. Deliberately read today's review, if present,
  only to retain window.since. Gather evidence
  for the resulting window through cited-retrieval. Fix one generated_at
  timestamp after retrieval, and publish the exact window, event_count and
  from_sha..to_sha it returned. A missing source is a failed collection,
  not zero events: signal_done failed and keep the previous review/result.
  Do not label a partial collection complete; if a cap prevents covering
  the window, fail and state the retrieval gap.

  Write sections in this order, omitting empty sections:
  What moved; Decisions and why; Waiting on you; Risks; Diffs worth reading.
  Every claim, including a reason or a risk, needs at least one citation to
  an item returned by cited-retrieval. Cut uncitable claims. A decision's
  reason must be recorded, never guessed. Avoid an uncited opening summary.
  Use a generic work-review format; no section or citation depends on an
  agent name, vendor, or application. event_count counts distinct events
  used, not citations or supporting files. If it is zero, sections is []
  and the only body line is "No recorded changes in this window."

  The result payload is {person, review_path, window:{since,until},
  generated_at, event_count, from_sha, to_sha, sections:[{title,claims:
  [{text,citations:[{source,org,team,at,path?,run_id?,sha?,id?,record?}]}]}]}.
  Use source commit/run/advance/story/message/inbox. A message is an agent
  update and carries record: agent-update; inbox IDs are separate. Story
  paths end in #Lnn. Use full commit SHAs. All citations stay in this org
  and team. Do not put summary text inside citation objects.

  Prepare the new review body and non-receipt frontmatter for this team's
  content/reviews/{{person}}/{{date}}.md before changing the existing file
  (review_path is reviews/{{person}}/{{date}}.md, relative to content).
  Frontmatter: person, generated_at, window_since, window_until, event_count,
  from_sha, to_sha, and the latest receipt fields when present. No type
  or cs:* fields: this is plain metadata, not a pipeline story. Follow it
  with the window, generation time, event count and commit range, then the
  nonempty sections and cited claims. Markdown citation labels include
  sha, run_id, path#Lnn or id explicitly. Commit citations link to the
  context repo commit; run/message/inbox citations retain their identifiers
  for lookup in the pane. A no-event review still keeps its metadata and
  has the single body line above.

  Immediately before writing the prepared replacement, re-read today's file
  and copy its current opened_at and acted_at fields into the replacement.
  If the file does not exist, there are no receipts to preserve. Preserve
  absence as well as presence: if a receipt field is now absent, leave it
  absent so an undo during collection is respected. Never restore receipts
  from the initial read.
  Do not gather more evidence or do other work between this fresh receipt
  read and the write. Replace today's file rather than append a second review.

  The agent does the git: stage only this person's review directory in the
  team context repo, including receipt-only edits to earlier days. Commit
  and push that repo with the user's git identity and explicit paths, then
  report_context_sync with this org and state ok. Never commit unrelated
  working-tree edits. If push fails, report_context_sync failed and
  signal_done failed; do not promote a new cached review. Do not create an
  empty commit if the desired review and receipts are already committed.
  After successful push, routine_publish_result with the exact payload
  matching the committed review, then signal_done success. CodeSense does
  not sync this repository for you.
where:
  kind: team_workspace
  machine: local
triggers:
  - schedule:
      cron: "0 7 * * 1-5"
      tz: America/Los_Angeles
policy:
  max_runtime: 15m
runs_on: one_mac
variables:
  person:
    type: text
    default: sam
revision: 1
result_schema: {
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "person",
    "review_path",
    "window",
    "generated_at",
    "event_count",
    "from_sha",
    "to_sha",
    "sections"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "person": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$"
    },
    "review_path": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^reviews/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*/[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\\.md$"
    },
    "window": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "since",
        "until"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "since": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        },
        "until": {
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time"
        }
      }
    },
    "generated_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "event_count": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "from_sha": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{40}$"
    },
    "to_sha": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{40}$"
    },
    "sections": {
      "type": "array",
      "maxItems": 5,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "title",
          "claims"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "title": {
            "enum": [
              "What moved",
              "Decisions and why",
              "Waiting on you",
              "Risks",
              "Diffs worth reading"
            ]
          },
          "claims": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": [
                "text",
                "citations"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "citations": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "required": [
                      "source",
                      "org",
                      "team",
                      "at"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "source": {
                        "enum": [
                          "commit",
                          "run",
                          "advance",
                          "story",
                          "message",
                          "inbox"
                        ]
                      },
                      "org": {
                        "const": "acme/team-context"
                      },
                      "team": {
                        "const": "web"
                      },
                      "at": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "format": "date-time"
                      },
                      "path": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "pattern": "^.+#L[1-9][0-9]*$"
                      },
                      "run_id": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "minLength": 1
                      },
                      "sha": {
                        "type": "string",
                        "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{40}$"
                      },
                      "id": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "minimum": 1
                      },
                      "record": {
                        "const": "agent-update"
                      }
                    },
                    "oneOf": [
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "commit"
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "sha"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "run"
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "run_id"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "advance"
                          }
                        },
                        "anyOf": [
                          {
                            "required": [
                              "run_id"
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "required": [
                              "path"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "story"
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "path"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "message"
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "id",
                          "record"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "properties": {
                          "source": {
                            "const": "inbox"
                          }
                        },
                        "required": [
                          "id"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "allOf": [
    {
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "event_count": {
            "const": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "then": {
        "properties": {
          "sections": {
            "maxItems": 0
          }
        }
      },
      "else": {
        "properties": {
          "sections": {
            "minItems": 1
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
